  "confirmed_interpretation": [
    "Greedy versus frequency changes the actual entry-node set on every query in all eight fixed cells; the explanation that selected portals never alter actual entry sets is ruled out for this saved pilot.",
    "Returned valid top10 ID sets nevertheless coincide on 68.34 to 93.36 percent of queries; exact ordered results coincide on 68.29 to 93.36 percent. This is final-output agreement, not trace or exploration agreement.",
    "Positive weighted fit-proxy exposure occurs for 98.34 to 99.53 percent of queries per structure. A simple absence of exposure to fit-proxy gains is not an adequate description of this pilot.",
    "All eight original global portal Recall intervals still include zero. Positive-exposure subgroup mean Recall changes have mixed signs; three are negative descriptively. These subgroup means have no new CI and do not establish significant subgroup harm or benefit.",
    "WebVid lambda1 has six undefined weighted-exposure queries at each L because positive oracle weight falls on a leaf with no fit support. They remain in the full totals and the undefined bin; do not replace their score with zero or count repeated L as independent samples."
  ],
  "not_established": [
    "Identical returned ID sets do not establish identical visited nodes, expansions, distances, paths or NDC. Aggregate mean NDC changes already show that final-output agreement cannot be used as an overall cost-equivalence statement.",
    "The single-entry independent-search union proxy versus joint multi-entry search mismatch is compatible with the observations, but redundancy, fit optimism, sample shift and search-path interactions remain unseparated hypotheses.",
    "An interval containing zero is not an equivalence or no-effect test. Tiny negative/zero/undefined exposure bins must not be selected as successful submethods.",
    "This same-lambda portal diagnosis does not isolate the cause of cross-lambda structure harm and does not identify a graph-connectivity bottleneck."
  ],
